<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guebwiller</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gebweiler</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guebwiller is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haut-rhin">Haut-Rhin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, at the entrance to the Florival valley of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a>. It was the main town of the territory of the prince-abbots of Murbach, who moved their seat there in the 18th century and built its neoclassical church of Notre-Dame. In the 19th century it became a centre of textile manufacturing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guebwiller.jpg" alt="Guebwiller" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Florival fr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guebwiller-St_Leger.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
